Why is the arbitrary value so high? 

```sh
bash-5.2$ cat a.c 
#include <unistd.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    printf("%d\n", sysconf(_SC_OPEN_MAX));
    return 0;
}
bash-5.2$ gcc a.c 
bash-5.2$ ./a.out 
1024
````

Did you get a `_SC_OPEN_MAX_`  higher than `1024` for a specific kernel version?

